# Bandit 6 → 7

Goal: find the password. It's somewhere on the whole server, owned by user `bandit7`, group `bandit6`, and exactly 33 bytes.

Not in the home directory this time — need to search the entire filesystem starting from `/`. `find` handles all three filters at once:

```bash
find / -user bandit7 -group bandit6 -size 33c 2>/dev/null


-- / starts the search from root
-- -user bandit7 matches files owned by that user
-- -group bandit6 matches files in that group
-- -size 33c matches exactly 33 bytes
-- 2>/dev/null sends error messages (mostly "Permission denied") to the void so the actual result isn't buried
-- That returns one path. Cat it:

cat /var/lib/dpkg/info/bandit7.password
